<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	Debug/local-dev entitlements for building on a free Apple Personal Team.

	A Personal Team cannot provision CloudKit containers, App Groups, push
	(aps-environment), or time-sensitive notifications, so every one of those
	keys is omitted here rather than being requested and failing to sign. The
	full set still lives in SquirrelTrap-Release.entitlements — switch Debug
	back to that file once a paid Developer Program team is signed in.

	What this costs at runtime, and nothing else:
	  - iCloud sync across Macs (CloudSyncEngine gets no usable container)
	  - the desktop widget's shared data (no App Group container)
	  - "time sensitive" delivery for reminder alarms (they still fire, just
	    without breaking through Focus)

	The core loop — Cmd+Tab prompt, the to-do list, Reminders sync, local
	notifications — needs no entitlement at all and is unaffected.
	-->
	<key>com.apple.security.app-sandbox</key>
	<false/>
</dict>
</plist>
